ath12k: qmi: take the firmware memory mode from the device tree

ath12k picks a memory profile from how much RAM Linux has and then sends
that same index to the firmware as mem_cfg_mode in the host capability
message. Those are two different things.

The host-side index selects ath12k_mem_profile_based_param[], which sizes
the driver's own rings and descriptor pools. mem_cfg_mode tells the
firmware which of its profiles to use. Downstream boards carry the value
the firmware expects in qcom,tgt-mem-mode and index qcom,bdf-addr and
qcom,caldb-addr by it, and on IPQ5332 the Xiaomi BE3600 Pro sets 2 -- a
value ath12k has no profile for, since it defines only 0 and 1.

Let the device tree override what the firmware is told while leaving the
host's own sizing alone, so a board can report the mode its firmware was
built for.

Signed-off-by: Hideo Sumi <hideo.sumi@mugops.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
@@ -3861,6 +3861,7 @@
 
 int ath12k_qmi_init_service(struct ath12k_base *ab)
 {
+	u32 tgt_mem_mode;
 	int ret;
 
 	memset(&ab->qmi.target, 0, sizeof(struct target_info));
@@ -3868,6 +3869,25 @@
 	ab->qmi.ab = ab;
 
 	ab->qmi.target_mem_mode = ab->target_mem_mode;
+
+	/* The memory mode reported to the firmware is not always the same
+	 * number as the host-side profile index.
+	 *
+	 * ath12k picks its profile from how much RAM Linux has and then
+	 * sends that same index as mem_cfg_mode. Downstream boards carry
+	 * the value the firmware expects in qcom,tgt-mem-mode, and index
+	 * qcom,bdf-addr / qcom,caldb-addr by it. On this SoC the vendor
+	 * sets 2, a value ath12k has no profile for at all.
+	 *
+	 * Let the device tree override what the firmware is told, while
+	 * leaving the host's own ring and descriptor sizing alone.
+	 */
+	if (!of_property_read_u32(ab->dev->of_node, "qcom,tgt-mem-mode",
+				  &tgt_mem_mode)) {
+		ath12k_warn(ab, "DBG: mem_cfg_mode %u from DT (host profile %u)\n",
+			    tgt_mem_mode, ab->target_mem_mode);
+		ab->qmi.target_mem_mode = tgt_mem_mode;
+	}
 	ret = qmi_handle_init(&ab->qmi.handle, ATH12K_QMI_RESP_LEN_MAX,
 			      &ath12k_qmi_ops, ath12k_qmi_msg_handlers);
 	if (ret < 0) {
